# Postgres connection string.
#
# Local development: run `docker compose up -d` (see docker-compose.yml),
# then use the value below as-is.
#
# Production (DigitalOcean App Platform): set DATABASE_URL to your Managed
# Postgres connection string. If the database is attached as a component, the
# binding ${db.DATABASE_URL} works (use it AS-IS — do not append extra query
# params like &schema=... or ?sslmode=...). TLS is handled in lib/prisma.ts.
# Never put the real value in this file or commit it anywhere.
#
# Optional, recommended for production: DATABASE_CA_CERT holds DigitalOcean's
# CA certificate (download it from the database's Connection Details page). When
# set, the app verifies the server certificate instead of skipping verification.
DATABASE_URL="postgresql://pdpsi:pdpsi@localhost:5432/pdpsi?schema=public"
